<!--
  GitTune - MSIX / Microsoft Store package manifest (source of truth).

  Identity values below are issued by Partner Center. Do NOT invent or edit them
  by hand; change them in Partner Center and re-download if they ever change.

    Package/Identity/Name                     OliverLin.gittune
    Package/Identity/Publisher                CN=A2A117EA-E7A5-4E7B-8905-441F8215E9A4
    Package/Properties/PublisherDisplayName   OliverLin
    Package Family Name (PFN)                 OliverLin.gittune_8q9a519brkbx0
    Package SID                               S-1-15-2-1630421473-1458451896-820385715-2649480046-476101059-3880151009-3782617673
    Store ID                                  9P3QDXV5HTBM

  The MSA app ID (ba343920-5c48-4a61-8afe-4408348bf41b) and the Store ID are
  Partner Center identifiers only - they do NOT appear in this manifest.

  GitTune is a full-trust Win32 desktop app (Rust + Slint), not a UWP app, so it
  declares EntryPoint="Windows.FullTrustApplication" plus the restricted
  capability "runFullTrust". The manifest and the built GitTune.exe must sit in
  the same folder of the package layout, next to Assets\.

  Version must be 4-part and match Cargo.toml's 3-part version + ".0"
  (Cargo.toml 1.3.2  ->  Version="1.3.2.0").

  AppxManifest.xml in this repository is byte-identical to this file: Visual
  Studio / MSBuild consume "Package.appxmanifest", while makeappx, the MSIX
  Packaging Tool, MSIX Hero and the Store uploader look for "AppxManifest.xml".
  Keep the two files in sync (or copy/rename this one at pack time).
